Nethack as it now stands has a hard limit for max score, which at the
moment can only be (realistically) reached by certain possibly abusive
tactics. So if score counts, the thing that counts most is getting
that maximum score. If score is really what people are interested in,
if you disable pudding farming, and rider farming, and quest farming,
and gremlin farming, and confused-create-monster acid blob farming,
and...., people who are motivated by score will just keep trying to
find other ways to get to that MAXINT number. You'll be chasing after
them forever.

If you want a score that says "X is a better player than Y", how are
you going to do that? If killing monsters gets score points, people
who try for "lowest kills" must be bad players? If having gold when
you die / ascend / escape gets score points, people who donate all
their cash for protection and fail to kill the priest must be bad
players? If having artifacts gets score points, people who play
atheist wishless must be bad players? No one number will be able to
capture all of the things that people have as goals in Nethack. This
is why I don't care much for the highscore list.

